WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:03.480
The last section of lore that we translated was in Izalith and

00:00:03.969 --> 00:00:08.219
what we learned there forever changed the way that I'll view it going forward.

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:12.659
Back then I also mentioned the Abyss and its creatures and,

00:00:13.269 --> 00:00:14.710
just like in Izalith,

00:00:14.710 --> 00:00:17.969
there's far more of these creatures than the English lets on.

00:00:18.430 --> 00:00:22.079
First and most importantly, the Primordial Serpents.

00:00:22.420 --> 00:00:26.580
So the very name Primordial Serpent is perhaps more accurately

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:33.299
translated as World Serpent, which is a really overt reference to the legendary world serpent Jörmungandr

00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:39.239
of Norse mythology. Jörmungandr is a child of Loki. He's a sea serpent

00:00:39.239 --> 00:00:44.519
that is so giant that his body encircles the entire Earth. Actually,

00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:50.069
Chester also refers to the Primordial Serpents as giant snakes,

00:00:50.530 --> 00:00:58.530
calling them Orochi in the Japanese text. So they're the biggest snakes in From Software history. Eh -eh, they were.

00:00:59.199 --> 00:01:05.548
The imagery of a snake eating its own tail is an example of an Ouroboros, a symbol of wholeness,

00:01:06.220 --> 00:01:11.369
infinity, the universe, the cycle of life death and rebirth, and these are all

00:01:11.740 --> 00:01:16.019
concepts that fit really neatly with the so called Primordial

00:01:16.330 --> 00:01:22.830
Serpents, because they're obsessed with the cycle of the world. And I think it's fair to take issue with the word "primordial";

00:01:23.380 --> 00:01:30.659
this implies that they've existed since the beginning of time, but a couple of item descriptions actually suggest that serpents are

00:01:30.970 --> 00:01:32.970
derivative of ancient dragons.

00:01:33.130 --> 00:01:34.180
No.

00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:38.909
Instead, these World Serpents are better seen as creatures that

00:01:39.430 --> 00:01:45.449
represent and understand the logic of the world. "I am the Primordial Serpent

00:01:45.970 --> 00:01:52.889
Darkstalker Kaathe. I can guide thee and illuminate the truth."

00:01:53.530 --> 00:01:57.570
"I am the Primordial Serpent Kingseeker Frampt,

00:01:58.149 --> 00:02:00.718
close friend of the Great Lord Gwyn.

00:02:01.329 --> 00:02:05.339
Chosen Undead, I wish to elucidate your fate."

00:02:06.159 --> 00:02:11.348
They are elders, sages who take up the role to inform and advice,

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:14.830
respected for their profound knowledge of the universe.

00:02:15.379 --> 00:02:23.349
Even if Kaathe and Frampt interpret that knowledge differently, Kaathe, the Serpent found after defeating the Four Kings

00:02:23.780 --> 00:02:24.700
believes...

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:30.459
"Lord Gwyn resisted the course of nature." And when Kaathe talks about the

00:02:30.980 --> 00:02:32.980
quote-unquote course of nature,

00:02:32.980 --> 00:02:38.259
he's perhaps better translated as saying the "World's Logic." In Souls,

00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:45.010
this "World's Logic" was supposed to be the fall of ancients to light and the fall of light to dark.

00:02:45.470 --> 00:02:53.169
This is the logic of the world and Kaathe and his ilk help us because they've come to understand that reality at its core.

00:02:53.750 --> 00:02:57.849
Therefore, Kaathe's retinue probably weren't always aligned with the dark;

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:04.629
In fact, Kaathe, when he talks, he talks about Gwyn as if he was on a very personal level

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:05.780
with him.

00:03:05.780 --> 00:03:09.369
He betrays his thinking, he betrays his secrets and

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:15.250
if Kaathe is indeed loyal to the World's Logic as he says he is, then it follows that

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:18.519
he was once all for Quinn's age of light and

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:25.630
maybe he even encouraged Gwynn's war against the ancient dragons. The Age of Fire was clearly dawning and,

00:03:26.150 --> 00:03:31.060
back then, it was only logical that it be dominated by beings of fire.

00:03:31.549 --> 00:03:37.179
But next, it was time for dark to prevail. "After the advent of fire

00:03:37.639 --> 00:03:44.949
the ancient Lords found the three souls, but your progenitor found a fourth,

00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:48.819
unique soul, the Dark Soul.

00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:56.169
Your ancestor claimed the Dark Soul and waited for fire to subside;

00:03:56.750 --> 00:03:59.649
Thus began the age of men,

00:04:00.169 --> 00:04:01.300
the age

00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:02.690
of dark."

00:04:02.690 --> 00:04:05.050
That last line is actually incorrect;

00:04:05.210 --> 00:04:12.669
It suggests that the age of dark began, once, but it didn't. Instead, in the Japanese text it goes on to say

00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:20.739
"Eventually fire goes out and only dark remains. In that case, it would be an age of you humans, of dark."

00:04:21.100 --> 00:04:22.940
And, It's true.

00:04:22.940 --> 00:04:29.230
Living is a weakness. And even the gods who were persons of fire are no exception to that rule.

00:04:29.870 --> 00:04:33.609
But, this age never came to be thanks to Gwyn.

00:04:34.280 --> 00:04:40.720
Lord Gwyn feared the logic of the world. So he made his own. This was The First Sin.

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:48.000
Once, the Lord of Light banished Dark, and all that stemmed from humanity.

00:04:48.470 --> 00:04:52.029
And men assumed a fleeting form.

00:04:52.940 --> 00:04:56.000
These are the roots of our world.

00:04:56.810 --> 00:05:03.130
Cursed with undeath and relying on kindling the fire to cure hollowing, man became

00:05:03.650 --> 00:05:09.820
intrinsically tied to Gwynn's Age of Fire. In time, many even came to believe in and love

00:05:10.340 --> 00:05:14.260
the cage of falsehoods that had been created around them.

00:05:14.900 --> 00:05:18.010
Peace grants men the illusion of life.

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:23.800
Shackled by falsehoods, they yearn for love, unaware of its grand illusion.

00:05:23.840 --> 00:05:26.890
Gwyn even convinced a World Serpent,

00:05:27.290 --> 00:05:32.349
Frampt the Kingseeker, that he alone had changed the logic of the world.

00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:39.640
So you can imagine having a World Serpent on his side would have lent a lot of credibility to his cause and,

00:05:39.919 --> 00:05:47.169
in a way, Frampt isn't wrong. Gwyn did do irreparable damage to the logic of the world.

00:05:47.810 --> 00:05:52.270
In retrospect, we realized that he ended up creating an Age of Fire,

00:05:52.340 --> 00:06:00.060
so endless that it ended up burning the world down to ash without ever truly passing over to dark.

00:06:00.370 --> 00:06:08.040
Though Frampt does experience a lapse of faith when he witnesses the first Dark Lord depose Gwyn

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:14.000
Let Kaathe and Frampt serve your highness.

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:15.310
In the Norse myths,

00:06:15.310 --> 00:06:21.720
Jörmungandr the World Serpent, is mortal enemies with Thor the God of Thunder, you can see the parallels here.

00:06:22.240 --> 00:06:25.019
So too, does Kaathe, the World Serpent,

00:06:25.540 --> 00:06:30.959
undermine Gwyn God of Thunder's rule in Anor Londo and in Oolacile, as well.

00:06:32.130 --> 00:06:34.519
New Londo is of particular interest;

00:06:34.920 --> 00:06:40.969
the name "New Londo" is clearly derived from "Anor Londo" and if we go off the elvish

00:06:41.490 --> 00:06:43.670
Sindarin translation, Anor Londo

00:06:44.250 --> 00:06:46.250
translates to Sun Haven,

00:06:46.560 --> 00:06:54.530
making New Londo a sort of young small haven. The Four Kings of New Londo were appointed by Gwyn and they received

00:06:54.630 --> 00:06:56.540
fragments of his very own soul.

00:06:56.540 --> 00:07:02.450
And it's yet another example of Gwyn sharing his authority and his soul with others in his own

00:07:02.850 --> 00:07:07.070
self-interests. In addition to this point the Japanese name of the Four Kings

00:07:07.620 --> 00:07:13.790
suggests that instead of Kings they're more like officials or at least public Kings, sort of

00:07:14.010 --> 00:07:17.839
ambassadors that were part of Gwynn's overall plan for control.

00:07:18.480 --> 00:07:24.890
As for the ghosts in New Londo, they align with this common Japanese perception of evil spirits,

00:07:25.410 --> 00:07:31.489
resembling those who die in a really sudden or violent manner, people who are not properly

00:07:31.919 --> 00:07:34.369
respected after death, and, you know,

00:07:34.380 --> 00:07:39.649
the residents of New Londo were drowned on mass by the healers in their community.

00:07:39.650 --> 00:07:46.340
So they fit that criteria because those were supposed to be people they trusted. Even the mountain of corpses

00:07:46.710 --> 00:07:51.830
below, release the heads of undead called a resentment or a grudge,

00:07:52.020 --> 00:07:58.310
which supports the idea that the residents are bitter and vengeful at how they were killed.

00:07:58.310 --> 00:08:03.320
It also explains how they were created and what a ghost really represents in Souls.

00:08:03.750 --> 00:08:10.190
There was definitely a decline in New Londo society after Kaathe introduced Lifedrain to the Four Kings,

00:08:10.440 --> 00:08:17.510
but it's debatable whether it was actually Kaathe's intention to drag the city into the Abyss.

00:08:17.970 --> 00:08:24.260
Because in the Japanese Kaathe clearly states that "they," meaning the Four Kings, failed him.

00:08:24.260 --> 00:08:30.899
He says, "Without understanding the value of truth, they were merely conceited in their power."

00:08:31.229 --> 00:08:37.588
He expected more from them. He expected them to pursue the truth, not just steal from others.

00:08:37.600 --> 00:08:43.828
And, this same disappointment would apply to Manus' Abyss in Oolacile, really.

00:08:44.500 --> 00:08:51.779
While Kaathe definitely said to the Oolacilians "Hey, Manus is underneath your society and he is the origin of all humans."

00:08:52.300 --> 00:08:58.979
Gough himself admits that Oolacile brought the Abyss upon itself, by defiling his grave.

00:08:59.560 --> 00:09:04.769
Kaathe didn't necessarily intend for them to dig it up and mess everything up.

00:09:05.050 --> 00:09:09.659
It's definitely clear that Kaathe was trying to learn about the world and he made mistakes,

00:09:09.880 --> 00:09:14.279
as he eventually worked towards his end goal of usurping the fire and,

00:09:14.890 --> 00:09:21.239
the most success that he had was when he created a Sable Church from the ground up, with its own

00:09:21.519 --> 00:09:23.519
ideology and its own goal,

00:09:23.589 --> 00:09:26.698
instead of just relying on others, this was more successful.

00:09:27.519 --> 00:09:33.869
Kaathe worked until his dying breath, till the very end. In the Japanese, Yuria says

00:09:33.869 --> 00:09:39.500
Kaathe, I have failed thee.

00:09:39.880 --> 00:09:45.449
He was as devoted to the world's logic as Gwyn was to defying it, and

00:09:46.029 --> 00:09:49.169
there's this great parallel with Norse mythology

00:09:49.329 --> 00:09:50.350
once again;

00:09:50.350 --> 00:09:52.329
Jörmungandr and Thor,

00:09:52.329 --> 00:09:58.649
Kaathe and Gwyn, in both stories, both of them fall to one another at the end of the world.

00:09:58.870 --> 00:10:04.919
Both stories are identical in that way, which is maybe more than mere coincidence? In the end,

00:10:04.959 --> 00:10:11.159
the world's logic doesn't go from light to dark, it simply burns out and ash

00:10:11.709 --> 00:10:13.600
inherits the world, and,

00:10:13.600 --> 00:10:19.260
with that in mind, who knows what awaits us if Dark Souls 4 is ever made.

00:10:20.050 --> 00:10:25.529
I owe huge thanks for this video to Lokey, who you've probably heard about by now;

00:10:25.560 --> 00:10:32.519
he's one of the best writers I've ever met. He was the translator who contributed much of the script this time around

00:10:32.700 --> 00:10:38.019
and, I won't have as much time for scriptwriting in the coming months. I'm sure some of you know why.

00:10:39.170 --> 00:10:45.039
So instead of making no videos at all, I've simply asked for a little bit of help. I hope you guys don't mind.

00:10:45.560 --> 00:10:52.359
Thank you Lokey and thank you Parry God for the footage, and thank you as always for watching, and I'll see you next time.

